SOLAR POWERED GROUND DRILLER FOR AGRICULTURAL PURPOSE

Project Description

In ancient days, soil digging for plantation was carried out manually by humans using traditional tools such as hand augers. This process required more time, physical effort, and human labour, especially for large-scale plantation.

To overcome these difficulties, this project proposes a Solar Powered Ground Driller for Agricultural Purpose. The machine uses solar energy to power a DC motor-driven auger mechanism, which drills holes in the soil for planting saplings.

The main aim is to reduce manual labour, save time, improve efficiency, and make agricultural plantation easier.

Objectives

- To reduce manual digging work.
- To save time during plantation.
- To utilize renewable solar energy.
- To develop a simple and efficient drilling mechanism.
- To reduce human effort in agricultural activities.

Working Principle

The solar panel converts sunlight into electrical energy. This energy is stored in a battery and supplied to a DC motor. The motor drives the auger drill bit, which rotates to penetrate the soil and create holes for plantation.

Main Components

- Solar Panel
- Rechargeable Battery
- DC Motor
- Auger Drill Bit
- Frame and Supporting Structure
- Motor Controller
- Connecting Wires

Applications

- Agricultural plantation
- Sapling plantation
- Gardening
- Small-scale farming